A||||3||qwikgta||T-Top ??  Is the "frame" strong enough for swap||||5||
Z||000000||qwikgta||03-15-2001||12:50 PM||||I have an 88 coupe with the C&C "factory" TTop.  What has putting this on the car done to the strength of the frame.  Will it take a 3.8 or V8 swap with no prob.  Will I have to do something diff to lift the body off the cradle. It has 64K miles and the TTops need to have new seals put on but I think it is still straight.   Thanks<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||03-15-2001||12:55 PM||||The T-Tops will be just fine with an engine swap.  C&C did extensive testing to prove to GM that it was a viable option for them.  GM never would have approved the T-Top as a factory ordered option if it was not as safe as a "normal" Fiero.  This is why it took GM 3-4 years to offer it as an option......they were just as skeptical as you are.  It is a very sturdy set-up. <P>You have nothing to worry about. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||03-15-2001||01:30 PM||||As long as B-pillar is intact and sturdily attached to the front windshield frame the rigidity would should not be effected.<P>As I understand in the space frame construction even the glass is a stressed member aiding in stability!||||reg||6
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||03-15-2001||07:21 PM||||There is a guy named Paul Vargas that has a v8 swap in a ttop formula on archies site.  check it out.  i dont think he has any problems.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>    <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">        <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||1
